# The hearth at the end of the hall of faces, which burns on nothing (docs/regions/castle_ravenloft_gates.md §2).
# Behind it is the hidden hoard (the Tarokka place castle_ravenloft_hidden_hearth). Three ways to put it out: shut
# the flue (no roll; loud: the hall's guardians wake, crg_faces_wake), holy water, or Arcana (both quiet). A failed
# Arcana check closes that way. Then the seam beside the firebox can be found (Perception DC 13) and opened.

~ start
if flag.crg_ever_hearth_out
Narrator: The firebox is cold and black. A draught breathes through a seam in the stone beside it.
-> END
endif
Narrator: A fire stands in the great hearth, tall and steady. There is no wood under it, no smoke above it, and no heat in front of it.
if treasure_at:castle_ravenloft_hidden_hearth
Narrator: Through the flames, the back of the firebox is not soot-black like the sides. It is clean stone, with a seam down one edge.
endif
-> choices

~ choices
* Look closer. -> look
* [if not flag.crg_hearth_arcana_failed] [Arcana DC 15] Find the spell that feeds it and unpick it. -> arcana_ok | arcana_fail
* [if item:holy_water] Pour holy water on the fire. -> holy
* Shut the flue and smother it. -> smother
* Leave it burning. -> END

~ look
Narrator: Every carved face in the hall is turned a little toward this fire, like people warming their hands.
Narrator: A flue lever hangs in the chimney's throat, rusted open. Under the grate, scratched into the stone, runs a ring of tiny letters.
interject class:wizard: The ring is the fuel. Someone bound it to burn on nothing. Break the ring and it has nothing left.
interject class:rogue: Or shut the flue and let it choke. Simple usually works.
-> choices

~ arcana_ok
set crg_hearth_quiet
set crg_ever_hearth_out
Narrator: You find the ring's first letter and its last, and draw a line through both. The fire goes out like a held breath let go. Nothing in the hall stirs.
-> after

~ arcana_fail
set crg_hearth_arcana_failed
Narrator: The letters slide away from your attention like fish. The fire leans out to lick your sleeve, and the ring knots itself tighter. You won't unpick it now.
-> choices

~ holy
take holy_water 1
set crg_hearth_quiet
set crg_ever_hearth_out
Narrator: The holy water hits the flames. They flinch, hiss, and are gone. Along the hall, the carved faces look somewhere else.
-> after

~ smother
set crg_ever_hearth_out
Narrator: The lever shrieks as it moves. The flue clangs shut, the fire chokes and dies, and every face along the hall turns to look at you.
-> after

~ after
Narrator: Cold air breathes out through a seam beside the firebox. There is room behind that stone.
-> END
